{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Base","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols18DirectedHypergraphP","text":"DirectedHypergraph","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/DirectedHypergraph","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"type":"heading","text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Edges.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" Positions "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< P_s"},{"type":"text","text":" are the source incidences, hyperedge by hyperedge in index"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order and within one in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"sourceIndices"},{"type":"text","text":" order, and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"P_s + q"},{"type":"text","text":" is target incidence "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"q"},{"type":"text","text":", in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"same order. A per-incidence array is indexed by edge position. A view is a snapshot, so its own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"positions never change, but they are valid for the hypergraph only until its next mutation:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the view of the mutated hypergraph numbers the incidences afresh (on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"inserting one cell shifts every later incidence by one)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"The LabeledGraph law.","type":"text"}]},{"text":" Every index member reads the base’s rows, shifted where they hold","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hyperedges: ","type":"text"},{"code":"successorIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is ","type":"text"},{"code":"outHyperedgeIndices(ofIndex: i)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"of ","type":"text"},{"code":"n + p","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" it is ","type":"text"},{"code":"targetIndices(ofHyperedgeAt: p)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"; ","type":"text"},{"code":"predecessorIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"inHyperedgeIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" plus n, or ","type":"text"},{"code":"sourceIndices","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". So graph algorithms run on the view without","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"hashing a vertex. The view does not offer ","type":"text"},{"code":"_withSuccessorIndexRows","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", whose contract needs edge","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"positions in row order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Costs."}]},{"type":"text","text":" As for "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceGraphView"},{"type":"text","text":": O(1) reads on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"IncidenceList"},{"type":"text","text":", which stores its"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"incidences; on another base a hyperedge’s incidence numbers are a range, O(1), "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges[q]"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"binary-searches and selects by rank, O(log m + ⌈n\/64⌉) on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":", and a vertex’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"outEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"inEdges"},{"type":"text","text":" is computed from "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"_memberRank"},{"type":"text","text":", O(d·⌈n\/64⌉) on"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"OrientedIncidenceMatrix"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/hypergraphs\/directedincidencegraphview"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"sections":[],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Hypergraphs"}],"symbolKind":"struct","externalID":"s:11Hypergraphs26DirectedIncidenceGraphViewV","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Hypergraphs\/DirectedIncidenceGraphView.swift#L42"},"title":"DirectedIncidenceGraphView","roleHeading":"Structure","role":"symbol"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed hypergraph’s incidence graph, read lazily from its storage: a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" on "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0 ..< n + m"},{"type":"text","text":" whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i < n"},{"type":"text","text":" is the hypergraph’s vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"index "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"i"},{"type":"text","text":" and whose vertex "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"n + p"},{"type":"text","text":" is hyperedge "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"p"},{"t